60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Candidate D, the Mobile Branch, addresses the bus link gap Yumi identified.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Yes, and the attendance data from May shows high demand in those outer wards.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,But the vehicle running costs overran last year. Is the budget stable enough for a new vehicle?,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,The partner-run groups show that community-led models work. Candidate A fits that pattern.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Candidate C, the Maker Workshop, has a tool certification gap. We lack the trained supervisor.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@George, the equipment budget was under last year. Could that cover the initial vehicle setup?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,The mobile service would reach people who cannot come to us. That is a strong argument.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"The grant terms are risky. If the grant ends, the operating budget must absorb the cost.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"Candidate B, the Digital Archive, has a history of incomplete indexing. I am hesitant.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"Candidate A relies on trained facilitators. We have volunteers, but no one to supervise them.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,The winter closures didn't stop the community halls. A mobile service could be flexible.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I support D. It solves the access problem directly.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,I am concerned about the long-term funding. But D has the strongest demand evidence.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,I prefer A because it leverages existing community partnerships. But D has better data support.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I am worried about the staffing for A and C. D might be easier to staff with existing volunteers.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I vote for D. It addresses the access gap and has proven demand.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I vote for D. It is the most direct solution to the transport issue.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,George,,"I vote for D. The demand is clear, and we can manage the budget risk.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,I vote for A. It builds on successful community partnerships.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I vote for D. It seems more feasible given our current staffing constraints.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
